BenefitPackage{
status*	string
readOnly: true
Status of the benefit package. It can be:

ACTIVE: The benefit package is active.
AWAITING_AGENT_SIGNATURE: The benefit package has been created and is awaiting the signature of the agent.
AWAITING_START: The benefit package has been submitted and is awaiting its active_start_at date.
CANCELLED: The benefit package has been cancelled by the agent.
DRAFT: The benefit package has been created but not yet submited.
EXPIRED: The active_end_at date has finished, and the benefit package is no longer active.
N.B. The list of values is temporary and still needs to be validated / settled on MyDataAtlas before the release of the stable version.

Enum:
[ ACTIVE, AWAITING_AGENT_SIGNATURE, AWAITING_START, CANCELLED, DRAFT, EXPIRED ]
benefit_package_id*	string
maxLength: 18
example: b09aac28-7f63
readOnly: true
Identifier of the benefit package.

product_reference*	string
maxLength: 10
example: I_C_BR
Short and readable concatenation of information related to the product.

active_start_at*	string($date)
example: 2028-05-22
Date when the benefit package effect takes place.

N.B. If the date is in the past, it will be set to today.

ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD).

active_end_at*	string($date)
example: 2029-05-22
Date when the benefit package ceases to have effect. ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD).

amount_of_policies*	number($integer)
minimum: 1
example: 12500
Estimated amount of policies that should be affected by the benefit package.

affected_policy_range*	{
description:	
Range of policy numbers affected by the benefit package.

external_number_start_at*	[...]
external_number_end_at*	[...]
 
}
